<view class="text">Service content: Clarify the specific products or services provided by the enterprise to users, including but not limited to product functions, performance, after-sales services, etc. User rights and obligations: stipulates the rights and obligations that users should enjoy when using products or services, such as providing true information, protecting account security, abiding by usage rules, etc. Enterprise Rights and Obligations: Clarify the rights and obligations that enterprises should enjoy in providing products or services, such as ensuring product quality and providing necessary technical support, etc. Fees and payment: If paid services are involved, the fee standard, payment method and payment time, etc. shall be clearly stated. Privacy protection: stipulates how companies collect, use, and protect users' personal information, and how users exercise their privacy rights. Liability for breach of contract: Clarify the responsibilities and compensation methods that both parties should bear when they violate the agreement. Dispute resolution: stipulates the resolution methods when disputes arise between the two parties due to the performance of the agreement, such as negotiation, mediation, arbitration or litigation, etc.</view>